WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:02.740
Film Courage: Who is buying short films today?

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.939
Daniel Sol, CoFounder of The Hollyshorts Film
Festival: That’s obviously the ever changing

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:13.290
question right now with steaming platforms
and apps and development and short content,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:19.030
short films where to place short films is
in the new world of streaming is sort of the

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.030
great unknown.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.710
It’s something we are excited about because
there is potential for shorts to be its own

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.020
big market and it’s something we are trying
to get behind and are really excited about.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.161
Outside of the big question or the broader
question there are specific companies that

00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:35.570
are looking for short content, we work with
a few of them.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.649
One of them is Dust, they look for sci-fi
films.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:43.760
The specific content they are looking for
is sci fi or sci fi adventure (that kind of

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.790
adventure).

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:53.200
So we like to talk with them and work with
them “Hey we have a great film, take a look.”

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.989
If they like it they can acquire it.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.910
So there deals are exclusive and are fair.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:04.769
It’s a win-win for everyone and they also
have a sister company or alternate company

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:06.220
Alter and Alter does horror films.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.220
So they look for science fiction or VHX but
they are looking for those films and we like

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.220
to work and talk with them all of the time.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.220
We have a great scoff film here, take a look,
they can acquire (non-exclusive), there deals

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.220
are fair and you get more exposure so there
focus is more horror/thriller.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:16.080
So they are both genre based but really cool
opportunities for filmmakers looking for exposure

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.810
and getting acquired in non-exclusive ways
so they are not taking your film or taking

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.310
the IP [intellectual property] or anything
like that.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:28.210
So it’s definitely a place for filmmakers
to get exposure and get distribution.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.720
And of course everyone knows ShortsTV, shortsTV
has been doing it a long time so they are

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.971
always acquiring shorts and they are on DirectTV
and AT&amp;T and all that stuff so they are on

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:40.009
television so that’s their area or angle.

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:43.560
They have been looking for shorts all the
time but they’ve been doing it for awhile.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.900
But they are now in the streaming aspect.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.060
The streaming aspect you see companies like
the Dust and then Crunchyroll does Anime.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:57.939
There’s all of these different apps or websites
that are focused on direct market so Anime

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:00.299
- Crunchyroll and sci-fi - Dust.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:05.659
There is a crypt tv app and they do horror
as well so there are all these different apps

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:09.269
and websites that are focused on certain genres
or styles of film that are looking to acquire

00:02:09.269 --> 00:02:14.309
films, all different shorts and things with
exclusivity and non-exclusivity.

00:02:14.309 --> 00:02:16.290
But now that’s a big deal.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.639
This is something that is every changing and
growing.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.659
This wasn’t the way five, ten, fifteen years
ago.

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:27.050
When we started there was noting, there were
no shorts distribution, there was none of

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.050
it.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.050
So there was no opportunity for shorts.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:34.400
There was no place in the distribution landscape
and now I’m just naming a few there are

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.140
just so many more that are doing this.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.769
So it’s pretty wild to think what can come.

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:42.449
There is stuff that is focused on certain
genres and there are apps that are looking

00:02:42.449 --> 00:02:46.299
for general short content and ever changing.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.819
We have our own platform that we are looking
to build up and work on.

00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:49.999
It’s called bitpix.

00:02:49.999 --> 00:02:51.632
So bitpixTV is the website and the app.

00:02:51.632 --> 00:02:53.430
We are on Amazon and Roku.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.099
We are looking to grow that.

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:59.569
Right now it’s a general shorts landscape,
we have shorts from all sorts of genres, everything

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:05.629
we have “Best of The Fest,” from the monthly
screenings and things from the platform (subscription

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:06.859
based).

00:03:06.859 --> 00:03:09.420
So that’s something that we’re looking
to do and take to the next level.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:17.040
We are not at that place where it is huge
or universally known (world wide) and everything.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.780
We feel we can get there because shorts are
a huge market because worldwide people like

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.659
watching shorts India, China, Europe…in
Europe they love shorts.

00:03:25.659 --> 00:03:30.159
Now if you have one place where everyone can
focus and go to and you thinking about streaming

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:31.669
certain TV shows - hey what about Netflix?

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:32.669
What about shorts?

00:03:32.669 --> 00:03:35.269
If we have the place where everyone says “Hey
I want to got to bitpix for shorts.”

00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:36.599
That would be pretty amazing.

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:39.909
If you can find all of the best shorts in
the world, they can find them there, that’s

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:44.180
something that we are exploring and it’s
something that the audience is now there more

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.859
than ever because TV’s are not TV’s anymore,
it’s your phone.

00:03:47.859 --> 00:03:51.870
You can sit on your phone and watch stuff
anywhere that you are and it’s something

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.439
that young generations are already doing.

00:03:53.439 --> 00:03:58.169
We are all trying to figure out how to capitalize
on this and make this be the next best thing.

00:03:58.169 --> 00:04:01.209
Maybe short content creators can make money
and have their shorts make money, can have

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:05.969
their shorts made and get a bigger audience
just some really cool festivals and some streaming

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:10.180
sites but be recognized worldwide in a different
way.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.109
And I really do think that this is where things
are going.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:17.139
I think in the next five to ten years it’s
going to be what the perception of what shorts

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:18.970
is (we talked about earlier).

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:19.970
What do short films mean?

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:20.970
What are shorts?

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:25.220
And 15 years ago it was just hey you made
a cool thesis film or art film and you tried

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.729
to show it at a cool festival, that’s all
that it was, it was strictly a calling card

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:32.860
and that film couldn’t make any money, that
film could be its own thing.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:37.820
Now there are so many places and avenues a
short film can go whether it’s distribution,

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:43.120
or a calling card, whether it’s a short
to be a feature, whether it’s you just make

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.840
great shorts and all you do is make awesome
shorts and that’s all you do.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:51.030
You don’t have to be just “I made a short
just to go make a feature film, to showcase

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.030
myself.”

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:55.610
No you can make great shorts and tell short
stories in a way that can be your calling

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:59.770
card, in that way not just to go onto tell
something else.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:03.300
This whole world with all of their different
apps and platforms that are looking for films,

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:09.009
it’s a good way to make some more money,
it’s a good way to get more exposure, it’s

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:10.009
huge.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:13.139
It’s definitely something that…it’s
just changed the whole landscape of what we

00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:15.090
are doing and that’s why we are seeing more
submissions.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.180
Not only the growth of the festival but the
fact that people are making more films than

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.060
every before in the world.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.139
It’s just a fact.

00:05:23.139 --> 00:05:24.390
Vimeo does their staff picks.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.520
Vimeo staff picks has their exposure, they
have that.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:34.060
There is Short Of The Week is the place where’d
they pick out the short, expose them and give

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.610
you a stamp of approval for your film and
that’s really cool.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:43.050
So you have these different sites and apps
that they are looking for content so now…not

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:49.680
just them but AT&amp;T are doing contests now
(they’ve done promos with us), so AT&amp;T is

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.340
looking for content for their channel as well.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:55.319
They are looking for shorts and they are looking
for short filmmakers to give them prizes.

00:05:55.319 --> 00:05:57.530
It’s sort of this new wild west, new world.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:02.009
There are actually new opportunities to not
just showcase yourself but make money and

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:07.860
also garner more exposure there to which is
really cool is to be part of that which is

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:11.560
something we couldn’t have foreseen back
then but now as we have positioned ourselves

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:15.630
as a strong festival and things in the short
space we want to see how we can push this

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:20.671
thing further and grow the online ad capability
and app capability and the festival and all

00:06:20.671 --> 00:06:28.380
of it to grow to new heights and make short
films be sort of a new premiere content.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:33.662
I think there’s a chance and I think that’s
pretty cool and I think in the next five to

00:06:33.662 --> 00:06:33.680
ten years we are going to see keep changing.

